  "query_preview": "(This evening through Saturday)...\nIssued at 139 PM EST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nSurface analysis this afternoon shows high pressure over MO and \nsouthern IL. This was resulting in a cool northwest flow across \ncentral Indiana. GOES19 shows some high, thin wispy CI pushing \nacross Indiana. The upper pattern across the United States was \ndominated by an upper low over WNY and another low just south of AZ. \nThis was resulting in Pacific upper flow streaming across much of \nthe country, streaming from the NW United States, across the Great \nPlains to the Ohio Valley and the Carolinas. Dew points across \nCentral Indiana were in the lower to mid 30s.\n\nTonight...\n\nDry weather will continue to be expected tonight. An upper level \ntrough will push across Ontario and the northern Great Lakes, but \nthis forcing will stay well north of Indiana. Meanwhile at the \nsurface, the strong high pressure system to our west will continue \nto build across Indiana. Forecast soundings and time heights \ncontinue to show a dry column with subsidence through the night. \nThus Mostly Clear skies will be expected along with lows in the \nupper 20s and lower 30s.\n\nSunday and Monday...\n\nMore dry weather with above normal temperatures will be expected on \nSunday and into Monday as we start the work week. Within the NW flow \naloft, a trough is expected to push across the Great Lakes tonight, \nbut any forcing with that system will remain well north of Central \nIndiana. Furthermore moisture remains an issued as high pressure \nsouth of Indiana blocks any gulf moisture. Time heights and forecast \nsoundings remain dry also. Thus a mostly sunny Sunday will be \nexpected. However a moderate pressure gradient will set up across \nthe area resulting in some afternoon wind gusts.\n\nUpper ridging will build across Indiana on Sunday night through \nMonday as the surface high pressure to the southwest rebuilds across \nIndiana. Again forecast soundings show a very dry column with ongoing \nsubsidence. Thus expect another sunny day with highs reaching the \nlower 60s.\n\nTuesday through Saturday...\n\nMainly dry weather will be expected through the week with the \nexception of late Wednesday through Thursday.\n\nModels show northwest flow in place across Indiana on Tuesday into \nWednesday with the main northern jet north of Indiana, across the \nGreat Lakes. Meanwhile high pressure over the northern plains on \nTuesday will be building east and passing across Indiana through \nWednesday. This will lead to continued dry and cool weather.\n\nBy Wednesday night and through Thursday, an upper trough is shown to \ndrop out of western Ontario and deepen as it pushes across the \nGreat Lakes and into Indiana with ample forcing available. An \nassociated surface low is projected to push across Indiana on \nWednesday Night and Thursday, as a cold front passes across the area \non late Wednesday night. With these features in play, Chances for \nrain will need to be included.\n\nBy Friday, Indiana will find itself on the backside of the departing \nlow and trough as a cool and strong area of Canadian high pressure \nbuilds across Indiana. Although an early, wrap around shower cannot \nbe ruled out on Friday, dry weather and cooler weather building \nacross the area will be the rule for Friday into Saturday, with \nbelow normal temperatures expected at that time.",
